  Bands should overlap: the top of band N must sit above the bottom of
  band N-1, or there are frequencies the VCO cannot reach. That is what
  the 60% varactor overlap is for, and it is the thing to check first.

  KVCO should be a few hundred MHz/V in every band, against 1458 MHz/V
  for the equivalent single-varactor design.

